./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:36:**F1-F2.** Both scripts bind evidence to `HEAD_SHA` but execute against the live worktree without requiring it to be clean. An uncommitted repair can make CI pass for code absent from GitHub; dirty contextual files can similarly hide findings from a reviewer. Refuse dirty worktrees before publication, or use an isolated checkout of the exact SHA.
./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:38:**F3-F4.** CI marks only step contexts pending, while `review.sh` trusts the old `local-ci/summary=success`. Review rerequests are worse: `gh_common.post_review` keeps the old body, while `post_summary` merely warns on publication failure. An old approved body and green status can therefore survive a newly adverse review. Invalidate summaries with a fatal `pending` write before reruns, replace the published ledger, and make final status publication fatal.
./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:48:**F10-F11.** `--adjudicated` checks only a prefix and current-head token; it does not establish four completed rounds or require checked, dispositioned findings and issue references. Gate 1 also accepts absent/null `draft`, contrary to `local/protocols/issues-prs.md:84-85`. Validate the complete adjudication record and require `draft is False`.
./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:50:**F12.** `post_merge` refreshes `origin/main` and starts the warmer even if `fast_forward_base` refused divergent history. That can make future diff audits use the wrong base. Continue alias refresh, warming, and cleanup only after verified fast-forward, or bind the alias directly to the verified fetched GitHub base.
./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:52:**F13-F14.** A change limited to `gh_common.py`, `wf_util.py`, `review.sh`, or `pr_merge.py` can produce eight skipped-success contexts without running `test_github_workflow.py`. Additionally, issue keys are optional, keyed adoption searches only 100 issues, and branch queries are not URL-encoded. Broaden workflow gating, require stable issue keys, paginate adoption, and encode query parameters.
./results/telemetry/reviews/pr7-a6889587acbd7e8e468b7c05aec95f159384582b.md:54:**F15-F17.** The issue quick-start omits its required body argument, while the PR quick-start permits a footer-only body despite the mandatory three-section template. Scout instructions still alternately require editing/committing an issue file and returning a GitHub comment; moved briefs retain dead `issues/briefs/...` links. Finally, the hook’s per-commit count and “split the change” advice contradict the normative 400-line per-episode cap. Align these operator-facing contracts before merge.
