./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785-code.md:35:**F1.** The source theorem `lem:ld-soundness` uses `\abc[\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}]` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:425-433`; `references/qpbt-paper/00_preamble.tex:311` expands that macro to consistency `\simeq_{\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}}`. The blueprint instead states all three conclusions using state-dependent closeness `\approx_{\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}}`. This is strictly weaker: `fact:agreement` at `ch12_qpbt_games.tex:227-234` only recovers consistency with the same error when both measurements are projective, while the produced `G^A,G^B` are merely POVMs. In particular, the third conclusion has no converse available. The mismatch is load-bearing because `ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:1195-1200` subsequently consumes self-consistency and point-measurement consistency. Restore `\simeq_{\delta_{\mathrm{ld}}}` in all three conclusions.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785-code.md:37:**F2.** The source’s `def:ld-meas` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:397-407` indexes outcomes by polynomial functions, and its parameter domain at lines 33-35 permits arbitrary positive `d`. The blueprint’s first measurement class instead uses formal representatives and incorrectly claims all chapter regimes satisfy `d \le q-1`. For allowed parameters `(q,m,d,k)=(2,1,2,1)`, `X` and `X²` are distinct representatives but the same function. Separate the source-facing function-indexed measurement class from the project’s representative-indexed Lean class.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785-code.md:39:**F3.** `docs/paper-gaps/policy.tex:248-252` and `docs/blueprint_style_guide.md:228-236` require blueprint bibliography entries to carry published PDF URLs, reserving repository paths for Lean comments and docstrings. The entries at lines 133, 143, and 153 violate that rule. The comment asserting a local exception does not amend either normative document.
