./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:50:F1. The construction in `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:303-320`, label `def:canonical-complement`, takes pivot columns from reduced row echelon form. Since RREF is unique for a row space, two bases of the same subspace give the same complement. Remove the basis-dependence claims here and at lines 141-142; dependence is only on the subspace and fixed ambient standard basis.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:52:F2. In `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:94-103`, label `lem:symmetric-strat`, the argument starts with a strategy for every `ε' > ε`. Neither it nor lines 110-122 produce a finite-dimensional strategy attaining `val*`, which line 74 defines as a supremum. State the approximate conclusion or supply an actual attainment theorem.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:54:F3. Primary label `lem:ld-sandwich` at `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:465-495` contains the same transposition, but the cited `references/neexp-paper/05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:952-973`, label `fact:low-degree-sandwich`, uses `G^k_{g_k}⋯G^1_{g_1}⋯G^k_{g_k}`. The current `G^k_{g_1}` is undefined when the outcome types differ; `k = 0` is also undefined. Apply the documented local correction and handle the empty case.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:68:F10. Source `fact:omega-anticomm-prob` at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:70-92` is inconsistent with the encoding defined at `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:873-897`. For admissible `(q,m,d)=(2,1,0)`, the actual anticommuting probability is `1/8`, while the second displayed lower bound is `1/2`. Require `d≥1` throughout and replace the false assertion that `ind_m(u)` vanishes exactly at zero.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:70:F11. The source at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:95-109` concludes only `A≈_δB`; the blueprint adds the exact sentence `‖(A-B)ψ‖²≤δ`. On a singleton distribution, `A=√(2δ)I`, `B=0` satisfies an `O(δ)` premise but violates that exact bound. Retain `O(δ)` or strengthen the hypothesis explicitly.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:72:F12. The public `lem:qld-win-implications` is unrestricted, but its proof establishes the conditional estimates only under `6md≤q` and then appeals to the later `thm:pauli`; the source has the same gap at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:244-258`. Moreover, `δ_qld≥1` does not trivialize the unsquared norm bound in `thm:pauli`. Prove the unconditional constant mass directly, for example from `ind_m(u)·ind_m(v)=∏ᵢ(1+uᵢ+vᵢ)` in characteristic two.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:74:F13. `def:ld-game` requires its dimension to divide `q`, but lines 898-906 instantiate it with `2m+2`; admissibility only gives `m | q`. For power-of-two `m≥2`, `2m+2=2(m+1)` has an odd factor and cannot divide power-of-two `q`. The same unsupported application occurs at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1278-1284`; a soundness theorem with a compatible sampler is required.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:76:F14. Source `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:917-924` defines `Dec` by replacing non-Boolean cube values with zero. For `q=8`, `m=d=1`, and constant `g=c∉{0,1}`, `Dec(g)=0` while `g(u)=c`. Lines 98-113 and 170-176 use this false identity, so the defect propagates through `lem:qld-construct-the-paulis`, `eq:qld-unitary-6`, `lem:qld-unitary`, and `thm:pauli`.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:78:F15. From `lem:twisted-commutation`, the exact phase is `(-1)^{tr(e_j e_{j'}(u·v))}` for every pair `j,j'`. Self-duality does not make this vanish after multiplication by arbitrary `u·v`. For odd extension degree at least three, take `u=e_j^{-1}` and `v=e_{j'}^{-1}` in one coordinate: the phase is `(-1)^{tr(1)}=-1` even when `j≠j'`. The source claim at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1451-1456` is therefore also false.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:80:F16. Source label `lem:qld-unitary` at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1765-1783` has the same gap. Without a small-`δ_S` condition, `1-2δ_S-√δ_S` can be negative and the EPR projection can be zero, making `aux₀/‖aux₀‖` undefined. Add a small-error case split and use an arbitrary auxiliary state with a trivial large-error bound in the other branch.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:82:F17. Existing `blueprint/src/chapter/ch03_preliminaries.tex:74-78` and `MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/Polynomials.lean:25-29` keep polynomial representatives rather than quotienting by evaluation. The new reduced-exponent function presentation identifies, for example, `0` and `X^q-X` when `d≥q`. Preserve the established representation or introduce a separately named evaluation-function object with the necessary restriction.
./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md:84:F18. Property 2 of `lem:qld-sublines` gives each projected point’s marginal separately, while `eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted` assumes a joint product distribution of both line-point pairs. The stronger joint law may follow from the construction, but it is not stated or proved. The source makes the same unsupported inference at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1241-1245`; remove this redundant route or prove the joint law.
