./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:292:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: pr150-terminal-typed-cl-followup -->\n## Context\n\nPR #150 proves the low-degree geometry and sampling identities from issue #106.\nIts terminal exact-head review found that the surrounding typed conditionally\nlinear (CL) claims still overstate what the linked Lean declarations prove.\nThis work is tracked separately so the reviewed geometry packet does not grow.\n\n## Mathematical scope\n\n- Prove the point-level conditional-linearity result for `ldPointCL` and a\n  common-level `IsTypedCondLinearFamily` theorem for the low-degree family.\n- Pair that family theorem with `ldQuestionDistribution_eq_typedCL`, so the\n  source-labelled low-degree typed-distribution result states both the CL\n  hypotheses and the distribution equality.\n- State and track the analogous source-faithful Pauli typed-family obligation;\n  do not advertise the existing equality-only theorem or its open proof as the\n  source lemma.\n- Reconcile the finite type-set hypothesis in the paper with\n  `IsTypedCondLinearFamily`: add the faithful boundary instance where needed,\n  or document a genuine generalization without giving it a source `\\leanok`.\n- Correct the Chapter 12 and Chapter 13 `\\lean`, `\\leanok`, and subordinate\n  obligation placement to match the resulting Lean statements and proof debt.\n\n## Sources\n\n- `references/qpbt-paper/07_types.tex:84-93`\n- `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:203-237`\n- `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:964-966`\n- `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1084-1120`\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The low-degree and Pauli blueprint nodes state exactly the corresponding\n  typed-family and distribution content.\n- Every statement/proof `\\leanok` is justified by a source-faithful completed\n  declaration; open obligations remain explicit and tracked.\n- No bridge hypothe