./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:488:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: pr151-round3-linearity-blueprint-followup -->\n## Context\n\nPR #151 proves the quantum linearity route, including the corrected bounds\n`2 * delta` for squared state-dependent operator distance and `delta` for the\nassociated binary-measurement distance. Its third exact-head review identified\nfive documentation and blueprint inconsistencies that must not expand that PR\nunder the owner's review-churn rule.\n\n## Required corrections\n\n- In `lem:qld-4-10` in `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex`, change\n  the displayed squared operator-distance bound from `delta_{x,z}/2` to\n  `delta_{x,z}`. The input to the corrected theorem is\n  `delta_{x,z}/2`, and its operator-distance conclusion doubles that input.\n- Update `docs/paper-gaps/qpbt_linearity-theorem-quotation.tex` so its account\n  reflects the proved `2 * delta` operator-distance theorem and the equivalent\n  `delta` binary-measurement theorem. Preserve its still-relevant discussion of\n  the common ancillary space.\n- Remove the transitive Fourier-square and one-measurement Naimark helper labels\n  from the statement-level dependency list for Boolean representation\n  stability; keep them in the proof dependency chain.\n- Replace the inaccurate uses of \"finite carrier\", \"ancillary carrier\", and\n  \"product carrier\" in the `Linearity.lean` and `Linearity/Stability.lean`\n  docstrings with finite-dimensional Hilbert-space terminology. Explain that\n  `Option (Fin t -> ZMod 2)` indexes an orthonormal basis of the ancillary\n  Hilbert space rather than being the Hilbert space itself.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The corrected blueprint bound agrees with\n  `exists_exactly_linear_observables` and with the normalization paper-gap note.\n- Both paper-gap notes give a coherent account of current proved status.\n- Blueprint dependencies are direct at statement level and complete in the\n  proof chain.\n- `leanbluep