./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:5051:  "body": "<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: workflow-wording-operator-vs-owner-vocabulary-sweep-from-d61adf30 -->\nFollow-up from the 2026-09-02 owner-stall audit (see EVOLUTION.md 2026-09-02 and issue #20 / PR #21). The layer says \"a human\", \"human attention\", \"human-invoked\", \"human-directed\", \"by hand\", \"a human's call\" in about a dozen places, meaning one of two different things \u2014 \"not the automated loop, use judgement\" (the operator qualifies) or \"the owner specifically\" (the operator does not) \u2014 and never distinguishes them. A GPT operator that classifies itself as automation reads all of them as the second and stalls. PR #21 fixed the sites on the PR #5 stall path; the rest are wording only and deliberately out of that episode's scope.\n\nSweep: replace the judgement sense with \"the operator\" and reserve \"the owner\" for the three briefing escalations plus `MIPSTARRE_INFRA_OVERRIDE`. Sites found (line numbers as of main at a7e5a38):\n\n- `local/bin/pr_merge.py:334` (post-merge divergence: \"resolve local main first, then rerun them by hand\"); `:312-314` \u2014 the CHANGES_REQUESTED remedy reads as a web-UI action; name the `gh_common` dismissal route or fix-and-re-review.\n- `local/bin/autofix.sh:598,604,606` residual \"by hand\"/\"human\" wording outside the cap note; `:521-524` the opt-in label message should name the enabling command.\n- `local/bin/agent.sh:3,199,205,209,211,282,333,341,351` \u2014 \"human-only\" guard wording; state that the guard is the `MIPSTARRE_AUTOMATION` / `MIPSTARRE_AUTOFIX_ACTIVE` env check, which blocks only calls from inside the review/fix loop, so the operator may use agent.sh directly.\n- `local/bin/ci.sh:744` (\"by hand\"), `:920-926` (axiom-audit warning: name the operator and the build lock); `local/bin/housekeeping.sh:451-452,464-465` (report-only wording: \"human-invoked\").\n- `local/protocols/autofix.md:88-90,178,308-313`; `local/protocols/review.md:252,256-257,298-302` (\u00a710 table row \"a human\" \u2192 \"a human or the operator session, never the review/fix loop\"); `local/protocols/ci.md:242,286-296`; `local/protocols/sessions.md:18,109,222`; `local/DESIGN.md:51,92-94,106`; `local/protocols/EVOLUTION.md:173-174` (conflict resolution \"remains the operator's decision\").\n- `local/protocols/review.md` has two sections numbered \"## 12\" (line 361 \"Deliberately not ported\" and line 379 \"Round cap and operator adjudication\"); `pr_merge.py` and `personas/main.md` cite \"review.md 12\" \u2014 renumber.\n- `docs/pr_review_management.md:11,26` \u2014 add a header note that rule 1 and steps 5-6 are superseded locally (merge authority is `pr_merge.py`; the adjudicating party is the operator per review.md \u00a712); drop the citation from `review.md:268`.\n- `local/protocols/autofix.md:161-170` vs `autofix.sh:557-609`: the cap ritual no longer claims to remove the label (fixed in PR #21); `autofix.sh:695` (`>=`) and the retired `pr_merge.py` comparison (`>`) differed \u2014 note the loop bound is `>=` in the doc.\n- `local/bin/main-session.sh:25-26,32-37` \u2014 already tracked by #15; when fixing it, point the launch prompt at `~/.codex/prompts/goal.md` / telemetry rather than at the owner.\n\nBudget: wording only, one commit, well under 400 lines; not a reason to touch code paths. Schedule after the next mathematics item (persona rule).",
