\\\\\\\\big)_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}\\\\\\\\mathsf{A}''}\\\\\\\\,,\\\\n   434\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   435\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\big(\\\\\\\\hat{Q}^{\\\\\\\\ell}\\\\n   436\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t_{[\\\\\\\\mathrm{eval}_{(x,z,\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\beta)}(\\\\\\\\cdot)=a]}\\\\n   437\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\big)_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}'}\\\\n   438\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\simeq_{\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{combine}}}\\\\n   439\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\big(\\\\\\\\hat{Q}^{x,z,\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\beta}_{a}\\\\\\\\big)_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{A}\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}''}\\\\\\\\,,\\\\n   440\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\notag\\\\n   441\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{gather}\\\\n   442\\\\t\\\\twhere the answer summation is over $a \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q$. Moreover, if $\\\\\\\\ell$ is\\\\n   443\\\\t\\\\taxis-parallel, then the outcome $f \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\deg_{d}(\\\\\\\\ell)$.\\\\n   444\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   445\\\\t\\\\n   515\\\\t\\\\tline-point distribution is precisely the statement that the left-hand\\\\n   516\\\\t\\\\tside of \\\\\\\\eqref{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}, averaged over\\\\n   517\\\\t\\\\t$D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Line}} \\\\\\\\times D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Line}}$, is at most $\\\\\\\\delta_P$.\\\\n   518\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{proof}\\\\n   519\\\\t\\\\n   520\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[The sub-line distribution]\\\\n   521\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-sublines}\\\\n   522\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:line, def:line-point-dist, def:ith-restricted-line}\\\\n   523\\\\t\\\\tThere exists a distribution $D$ over tuples $(\\\\\\\\ell, \\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z)$,\\\\n   524\\\\t\\\\twhere $\\\\\\\\ell$ is a line in $\\\\\\\\F_q^{2m+2}$ and $\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z$ are lines in\\\\n   525\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\F_q^m$, with the following properties:\\\\n   526\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}\\\\n   527\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\item The marginal distribution over $\\\\\\\\ell$ is the same as the\\\\n   528\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tmarginal of the line-point distribution over $\\\\\\\\F_q^{2m+2}$.\\\\n   529\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\item For any point of the form $u = (u_X, u_Z, \\\\\\\\alpha, \\\\\\\\beta)$\\\\n   530\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tlying on $\\\\\\\\ell$, it holds that $u_X \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\ell_X$ and\\\\n   531\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$u_Z \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\ell_Z$. Moreover, for $u$ chosen uniformly at random on\\\\n   532\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ell$, the marginal distribution over $(\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z, u_X)$\\\\n   533\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t(resp.\\\\\\\\ over $(\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z, u_Z)$) is such that the marginal over\\\\n   534\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$(\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z)$ is a mixture of the product distributions\\\\n   535\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ALine},i} \\\\\\\\times D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ALine},j}$ and\\\\n   536\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{DLine},i} \\\\\\\\times D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{DLine},j}$ for\\\\n   537\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$i, j \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{1, \\\\\\\\dots, m\\\\\\\\}$, and, conditioned on\\\\n   538\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t$(\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z)$, the point $u_X$ is uniformly random on $\\\\\\\\ell_X$\\\\n   539\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t(resp.\\\\\\\\ $u_Z$ is uniformly random on $\\\\\\\\ell_Z$).\\\\n   540\\\\t\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\item If $\\\\\\\\ell$ is axis-parallel, then $\\\\\\\\ell_X$ and $\\\\\\\\ell_Z$ are\\\\n   541\\\\t\\\\t\\\\taxis-parallel.\\\\n   542\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{enumerate}\\\\n   543\\\\t\\\\t(Property~3 is not part of the numbered statement in the source; see\\\\n   544\\\\t\\\\tRemark~\\\\\\\\ref{rem:qld-sublines-property-three}.)\\\\n   545\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n   546\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{proof}\\\\n   547\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:line-representative, def:ld-question-distribution,\\\\n   548\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tdef:line-point-dist, def:ith-restricted-line}\\\\n   549\\\\t\\\\tThe distribution $D$ is described by a sampling procedure. First sample\\\\n   550\\\\t\\\\t$(\\\\\\\\ell, u)$ from the line-point distribution over $\\\\\\\\F_q^{2m+2}$ and write\\\\n   551\\\\t\\\\t$u = (u_X, u_Z, \\\\\\\\alpha, \\\\\\\\bet