a uniformly random point $u_X$ on $\\\\\\\\ell_X$ (resp.\\\\\\\\ $u_Z$ on\\\\n   573\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ell_Z$), and a case analysis over $j$ shows that the marginal over\\\\n   574\\\\t\\\\t$(\\\\\\\\ell_X, \\\\\\\\ell_Z)$ is a mixture of the required product distributions:\\\\n   575\\\\t\\\\tfor instance, in the axis-parallel case with $1 \\\\\\\\le j \\\\\\\\le m$, the\\\\n   576\\\\t\\\\tmarginal over $(\\\\\\\\ell_X, u_X)$ conditioned on $j$ equals\\\\n   577\\\\t\\\\t$D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ALine},j}$, and even conditioned on $(\\\\\\\\ell_X, u_X)$ the line\\\\n   578\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ell_Z$ is distributed as $D_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{ALine},i_Z}$ for uniformly random\\\\n   579\\\\t\\\\t$i_Z$; the remaining cases are analogous, differing only in how the\\\\n   580\\\\t\\\\tindices are chosen. This gives Property~2. Property~3 is immediate from\\\\n   790\\\\t\\\\ta valid POVM; the polynomial $\\\\\\\\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ of\\\\n   791\\\\t\\\\tDefinition~\\\\\\\\ref{def:combine-map} is well defined here because Property~2\\\\n   792\\\\t\\\\tof Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} guarantees that $\\\\\\\\ell_X$ and $\\\\\\\\ell_Z$\\\\n   793\\\\t\\\\tare compatible with $\\\\\\\\ell$. If $\\\\\\\\ell$ is axis-parallel, then by\\\\n   794\\\\t\\\\tProperty~3 of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-sublines} so are $\\\\\\\\ell_X$ and\\\\n   795\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\ell_Z$, hence $f_X, f_Z \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\deg_d$ by Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-xz-lines};\\\\n   796\\\\t\\\\talong such a line either $(\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\beta)$ is constant, in which case\\\\n   797\\\\t\\\\t$f = \\\\\\\\mathrm{combine}_{f_X,f_Z}$ is a fixed linear combination of\\\\n   798\\\\t\\\\tpolynomials of degree at most $d$, or $(x,z)$ is constant, in which case\\\\n   799\\\\t\\\\t$f$ is affine in the line parameter, so in either case\\\\n   800\\\\t\\\\t$f \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\deg_d(\\\\\\\\ell)$. Chaining Lemmas~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:claim-17-1},\\\\n   801\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\ref{lem:claim-17-2} and~\\\\\\\\ref