Q}^\\\\\\\\line_{[\\\\\\\\eval_{(x,z,\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\beta)}(\\\\\\\\cdot) = a]})_{\\\\\\\\bob \\\\\\\\bob'} \\\\\\\\simeq_{\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\combine}} ( \\\\\\\\hat{Q}^{x,z,\\\\\\\\alpha,\\\\\\\\beta}_{a} )_{\\\\\\\\alice \\\\\\\\bob''}\\\\\\\\;,\\\\n  1032\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{gather}\\\\n  1033\\\\twhere the answer summation is over $a \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\F_q$. Moreover, if $\\\\\\\\line$ is axis-parallel, then the outcome $f \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\deg_{d}(\\\\\\\\line)$.\\\\n  1034\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{lemma}\\\\n  1035\\\\t\\\\n  1036\\\\tBefore proving the lemma we give definitions regarding distributions over lines and points.\\\\n  1037\\\\t\\\\n  1038\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{definition}\\\\\\\\label{def:ith-restricted-line}\\\\n  1039\\\\t  For any $i \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{1, \\\\\\\\dots,\\\\n  1040\\\\t  m\\\\\\\\}$ the \\\\\\\\emph{$i$-th restricted axis parallel line distribution $D_{\\\\\\\\ALine,\\\\n  1060\\\\t    \\\\\\\\E_{(\\\\\\\\line_X, x) \\\\\\\\sim D_{\\\\\\\\tvar_1, i}} \\\\\\\\E_{(\\\\\\\\line_Z, z) \\\\\\\\sim D_{\\\\\\\\tvar_2, j}} \\\\\\\\sum_{f_X, f_Z} \\\\\\\\bra{\\\\\\\\hat{\\\\\\\\psi}} (T^{\\\\\\\\line_X, \\\\\\\\line_Z}_{f_X, f_Z})_{\\\\\\\\alice \\\\\\\\alice'} \\\\\\\\ot (I - (\\\\\\\\hat{Q}^{x,z}_{f_X(x), f_Z(z)}))_{\\\\\\\\bob \\\\\\\\alice''} \\\\\\\\ket{\\\\\\\\hat{\\\\\\\\psi}} = O(m^2 \\\\\\\\delta_P)\\\\\\\\;. \\\\\\\\label{eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted}\\\\n  1061\\\\t    \\\\\\\\end{equation}\\\\n  1062\\\\t\\\\n  1063\\\\t    \\\\\\\\begin{lemma}\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-sublines}\\\\n  1064\\\\t      There exists a distribution $D$ over tuples $(\\\\\\\\line, \\\\\\\\line_X, \\\\\\\\line_Z)$ with the following properties:\\\\n  1065\\\\t      \\\\\\\\begin{enumerate}\\\\n  1066\\\\t      \\\\\\\\item The marginal distribution over $\\\\\\\\line$ is the same as the marginal of the line-point distribution over $\\\\\\\\F_q^{2m+2}$.\\\\n  1067\\\\t\\\\\\\\item For any point of the form $u = (u_X, u_Z, \\\\\\\\alpha, \\\\\\\\beta)$ lying on $