m that its proof only approximates.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F3 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:343` — `lem:ld-sandwich` pairs outcomes with the wrong measurements and is ill-typed.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F4 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:500` — `def:graph-distribution` divides by zero for an empty graph.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F5 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:90` — `def:ld-win-predicate` is undefined on diagonal questions with zero direction.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F6 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:132` — The Reed–Solomon parameters used to justify `lem:ld-soundness` have the wrong distance and omit the degree range.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F7 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:235` — `def:pauli-question-distribution` omits the admissible-field hypothesis needed to define its field and trace operations.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F8 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:262` — The Pauli question sampler is not the graph distribution it claims to instantiate.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F9 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:402` — The proof of `lem:delta-bound` uses the false implication `k ≤ m`.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [ ] F10 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:101` — `fact:omega-anticomm-prob` is false for the permitted case `d = 0`.\\\\n- [-] F11 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:159` — `lem:avg-closeness` strengthens an `O(δ)` hypothesis to an exact bound with constant one.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F12 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:368` — `lem:qld-win-implications` discards an uncovered parameter branch by circularly invoking the final theorem.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [ ] F13 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:898` — `lem:qld-4-7` applies classical soundness at a dimension that need not divide the field size.\\\\n- [-] F14 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:15` — The claimed decoder interpolation identity is false and is used throughout the extraction proof.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F15 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:63` — The asserted cross-basis commutation relation omits the actual trace phase.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [-] F16 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:198` — `lem:qld-unitary` normalizes a projected vector without proving that it is nonzero.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [ ] F17 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:309` — `def:polynomials-degree` conflicts with the established polynomial-representative interpretation of `polyfunc`.\\\\n- [-] F18 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:809` — The alternative consistency estimate uses separate marginals where a joint product law is required.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\\\n- [ ] F19 (changes) `prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/pr.md:19` — The required Motivation, Description, and Testing sections remain empty template comments.\\\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\\\n\\\\n## Review\\\\n\\\\nChanges are required. Several defects are inherited from the QPBT paper, but the blueprint currently presents them as valid definitions, lemmas, or proofs. Those cases need a policy-compliant local correction and paper-gap verdict rather than silently copying the defect.\\\\n\\\\nF1. The construction in `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:303-320`, label `def:canonical-complement`, takes pivot columns from reduced row echelon form. Since RREF is unique for a row space, two bases of the same subspace give the same complement. Remove the basis-dependence claims here and at lines 141-142; dependence is only on the subspace and fixed ambient standard basis.\\\\n\\\\nF2. In `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:94-103`, label `lem:symmetric-strat`, the argument starts with a strategy for every `ε' > ε`. Neither it nor lines 110-122 produce a finite-dimensional strategy attaining `val*`, which line 74 defines as a supremum. State the approximate conclusion or supply an actual attainment theorem.\\\\n\\\\nF3. Primary label `lem:ld-sandwich` at `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:465-495` contains the same transposition, but the cited `references/neexp-paper/05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:952-973`, label `fact:low-degree-sandwich`, uses `G^k_{g_k}⋯G^1_{g_1}⋯G^k_{g_k}`. The current `G^k_{g_1}` is undefined when the outcome types differ; `k = 0` is also undefined. Apply the documented local correction and handle the empty case.\\\\n\\\\nF4. Source label `def:graph-distribution` at `references/qpbt-paper/07_types.tex:65-82` has the same boundary omission. With no edges, `m = k = 0`, so `1/(2m-k)` is undefined and the displayed mass is not a probability distribution. Require a nonempty edge set.\\\\n\\\\nF5. The paper explicitly permits zero directions at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:106-116` and samples them at lines 230-237, while its predicate at lines 380-384 asks for “the” `t` satisfying `x=u₀+tv'`. When `v'=0`, every `t` works and a dishonest nonconstant answer gives different values. Specify a canonical zero-direction branch or change and rejustify the distribution.\\\\n\\\\nF6. `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:442-457` prints the same erroneous Reed–Solomon claim. Degree-at-most-`d` evaluation on all `q` points has parameters `[q,d+1,q-d]` when `d<q`, not `[q,d+1,q-d+1]`; for `d≥q`, even the dimension claim fails. Correct the provider argument and split the parameter regimes.\\\\n\\\\nF7. Source `def:admissible` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:958-960` requires both an admissible binary field size and `m | q`. Line 235 instead quantifies arbitrary naturals and assumes only divisibility, allowing values for which `F_q` or `tr_{q→2}` is unavailable. Scope the distribution, predicate, and completeness result to an admissible tuple.\\\\n\\\\nF8. Source `def:graph-distribution` assigns equal mass `1/(2m-k)` to every ordered supported pair. Sampling an undirected edge uniformly and then orienting it assigns loops mass `1/m` and oriented nonloops mass `1/(2m)`, which differs whenever loops occur; this graph has a loop at every vertex. Sample uniformly from ordered support.\\\\n\\\\nF9. Source label `lem:delta-bound` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:1520-1558` makes the same unsupported comparison. For allowed `a=1`, `b=1/2`, hence `c=4`, and `R=5`, the definitions give `k=9` and `m=8`. Bound `2^{-bm}` directly using `m ≥ (c/2) log R`; the lemma appears salvageable without `k≤m`.\\\\n\\\\nF10. Source `fact:omega-anticomm-prob` at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:70-92` is inconsistent with the encoding defined at `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:873-897`. For admissible `(q,m,d)=(2,1,0)`, the actual anticommuting probability is `1/8`, while the second displayed lower bound is `1/2`. Require `d≥1` throughout and replace the false assertion that `ind_m(u)` vanishes exactly at zero.\\\\n\\\\nF11. The source at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:95-109` concludes only `A≈_δB`; the blueprint adds the exact sentence `‖(A-B)ψ‖²≤δ`. On a singleton distribution, `A=√(2δ)I`, `B=0` satisfies an `O(δ)` premise but violates that exact bound. Retain `O(δ)` or strengthen the hypothesis explicitly.\\\\n\\\\nF12. The public `lem:qld-win-implications` is unrestricted, but its proof establishes the conditional estimates only under `6md≤q` and then appeals to the later `thm:pauli`; the source has the same gap at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:244-258`. Moreover, `δ_qld≥1` does not trivialize the unsquared norm bound in `thm:pauli`. Prove the unconditional constant mass directly, for example from `ind_m(u)·ind_m(v)=∏ᵢ(1+uᵢ+vᵢ)` in characteristic two.\\\\n\\\\nF13. `def:ld-game` requires its dimension to divide `q`, but lines 898-906 instantiate it with `2m+2`; admissibility only gives `m | q`. For power-of-two `m≥2`, `2m+2=2(m+1)` has an odd factor and cannot divide power-of-two `q`. The same unsupported application occurs at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1278-1284`; a soundness theorem with a compatible sampler is required.\\\\n\\\\nF14. Source `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:917-924` defines `Dec` by replacing non-Boolean cube values with zero. For `q=8`, `m=d=1`, and constant `g=c∉{0,1}`, `Dec(g)=0` while `g(u)=c`. Lines 98-113 and 170-176 use this false identity, so the defect propagates through `lem:qld-construct-the-paulis`, `eq:qld-unitary-6`, `lem:qld-unitary`, and `thm:pauli`.\\\\n\\\\nF15. From `lem:twisted-commutation`, the exact phase is `(-1)^{tr(e_j e_{j'}(u·v))}` for every pair `j,j'`. Self-duality does not make this vanish after multiplication by arbitrary `u·v`. For odd extension degree at least three, take `u=e_j^{-1}` and `v=e_{j'}^{-1}` in one coordinate: the phase is `(-1)^{tr(1)}=-1` even when `j≠j'`. The source claim at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1451-1456` is therefore also false.\\\\n\\\\nF16. Source label `lem:qld-unitary` at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1765-1783` has the same gap. Without a small-`δ_S` condition, `1-2δ_S-√δ_S` can be negative and the EPR projection can be zero, making `aux₀/‖aux₀‖` undefined. Add a small-error case split and use an arbitrary auxiliary state with a trivial large-error bound in the other branch.\\\\n\\\\nF17. Existing `blueprint/src/chapter/ch03_preliminaries.tex:74-78` and `MIPStarRE/LDT/Preliminaries/Polynomials.lean:25-29` keep polynomial representatives rather than quotienting by evaluation. The new reduced-exponent function presentation identifies, for example, `0` and `X^q-X` when `d≥q`. Preserve the established representation or introduce a separately named evaluation-function object with the necessary restriction.\\\\n\\\\nF18. Property 2 of `lem:qld-sublines` gives each projected point’s marginal separately, while `eq:qld-xz-lines-restricted` assumes a joint product distribution of both line-point pairs. The stronger joint law may follow from the construction, but it is not stated or proved. The source makes the same unsupported inference at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1241-1245`; remove this redundant route or prove the joint law.\\\\n\\\\nF19. The PR record contains only template comments. Populate the required sections with the QPBT source ranges, the declarations introduced, known paper discrepancies, and the actual validation commands.\\\\n\\\\nNo Lean source or blueprint `\\\\\\\\lean`/`\\\\\\\\leanok` links changed, and the changed chapters contain no direct `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, or proof-integrity bypass. I did not rerun the build under the read-only review contract; the PR record reports successful local CI. Residual risk remains in externally imported Ji–Natarajan–Vidick–Wright–Yuen and Coladangelo–Stark results, which were checked only as represented by the in-repository source mirrors.\\\\n\\\\n## Verdict\\\\n\\\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\\\n