o the decomposition invoked by the\\\\n   855\\\\t\\\\tsource is not established there. The proof above therefore uses only\\\\n   856\\\\t\\\\tthe first route, whose bound is dominated by the stated form\\\\n   857\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{combine}} = \\\\\\\\poly(m^2\\\\\\\\eps, md/q)$ since\\\\n   858\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_P = \\\\\\\\poly(\\\\\\\\eps, md/q)$, $\\\\\\\\delta_Q = \\\\\\\\poly(\\\\\\\\eps)$ and\\\\n   859\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Line}} = \\\\\\\\poly(\\\\\\\\eps)$. In addition, the final line of\\\\n   860\\\\t\\\\tthe source proof of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:claim-17-2} asserts the bound\\\\n   861\\\\t\\\\t$O(m^2\\\\\\\\delta_{\\\\\\\\mathrm{Line}})$ for a consistency term that is close to\\\\n   862\\\\t\\\\tone rather than for its deficit; the statements and sketches above\\\\n   863\\\\t\\\\trecord the corrected assertions.\\\\n   864\\\\t\\\\\\\\end{remark}\\\\n   865\\\\t\\\\n   866\\\\tThe measurements of Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-12} and Lemma~\\\\\\\\ref{lem:qld-4-13}\\\\n   867\\\\tconstitute a strategy for the classical low individual degree game in $2m+2$\\\\n   868\\\\tvariables. Applying the quantum soundness of that game yields a single\\\\n   869\\\\tprojective measurement whose outcomes are pairs of global polynomials.\\\\n   870\\\\t\\\\n   871\\\\t\\\\\\\\begin{lemma}[The global polynomial-pair measurement]\\\\n   872\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\label{lem:qld-4-7}\\\\n   873\\\\t\\\\t\\\\\\\\uses{def:polyfunc, def:expanded-state, def:expanded-point-measurement,\\\\n   874\\\\t\\\\t\\\\tdef:consistency, def:bracket}\\\\n   875\\\\t\\\\tThere exists a function\\\\n   876\\\\t\\\\t$\\\\\\\\delta_S(\\\\\\\\eps,m,d,q) = a(md)^a(\\\\\\\\eps^b + q^{-b} + 2^{-bmd})$, for some\\\\n   877\\\\t\\\\tuniversal constants $a > 1$ and $0 < b < 1$, such that the following\\\\n   878\\\\t\\\\tholds. For $\\\\\\\\hilb \\\\\\\\in \\\\\\\\{\\\\\\\\hilb_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{A}}, \\\\\\\\hilb_{\\\\\\\\mathsf{B}}\\\\\\\\}$ there\\\\n   