\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"## Findings\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:531` — `def:typed-cl-distributions` samples from `μ_G` without the nonempty-edge condition needed to define it.\\\\n- [ ] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:342` — `lem:ld-sandwich` uses an undefined uniform law and post-processing outside the chapter's finite-outcome API.\\\\n- [ ] F3 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:253` — The proofs of `fact:add-a-proj2` and `lem:cool-closeness-fact` erase hidden constants and claim exact `≤ δ` bounds.\\\\n- [ ] F4 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:19` — `def:ld-game` does not preserve the source-positive `d,k ≥ 1` domain, making `lem:ld-soundness` false at `d=0`.\\\\n- [ ] F5 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:146` — `lem:ld-soundness` imports tensor-code soundness after changing the zero-direction predicate without proving a transfer.\\\\n- [ ] F6 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:242` — `def:admissible` drops `d ≥ 1`, making Pauli completeness and `thm:pauli` false at `d=0`.\\\\n- [ ] F7 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:49` — `def:ideg-deg-polynomials` quotients coefficient outcomes into geometric functions and loses zero-direction answer data.\\\\n- [ ] F8 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:271` — `lem:povm-to-obs` and `lem:qld-comm-line-cons` replace asymptotic `O(δ)` estimates by unjustified constant-one inequalities.\\\\n- [ ] F9 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:562` — The sampler for `lem:qld-sublines` misstates the diagonal direction law and does not establish its claimed exact marginals.\\\\n- [ ] F10 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:816` — The retained proof of `lem:qld-4-13` does not imply the advertised `poly(m²ε,md/q)` error dependence.\\\\n- [ ] F11 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:928` — `lem:qld-4-7` applies classical soundness at dimension `2m+2` without its required divisibility hypothesis.\\\\n- [ ] F12 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:281` — The proof of `thm:pauli` skips the range-projection transfer from the swap unitary to the defined local isometry.\\\\n- [ ] F13 (changes) `prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/pr.md:41` — The PR says six bibliography entries were added, but the diff adds five.\\\\n- [ ] F14 (changes) `prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/pr.md:52` — The Testing section records CI for the previous head rather than current head `99d235c`.\\\\n\\\\n## Review\\\\n\\\\nChanges are required. Twelve mathematical blockers remain, several inherited from the paper but currently presented as completed definitions or proofs.\\\\n\\\\nF1. `def:graph-distribution` now correctly requires a nonempty edge set, but `def:typed-cl-distributions` accepts an arbitrary graph and immediately invokes `μ_G`. The source has the same implicit boundary omission at `references/qpbt-paper/07_types.tex:65-92`, label `def:graph-distribution`, where the normalization is `1/(2m-k)`. Propagate `E ≠ ∅` to the typed definition and downstream uses.\\\\n\\\\nF2. `lem:ld-sandwich` samples uniformly from `Y` without assuming it finite and nonempty. It also post-processes into arbitrary `R_i`, while `def:bracket` at lines 28-38 requires a finite target. The omission is inherited from `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:465-495`, label `lem:ld-sandwich`; the cited `references/neexp-paper/05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:952-973`, label `fact:low-degree-sandwich`, instead uses a specified probability distribution. Add the boundary hypotheses or use finite evaluation images.\\\\n\\\\nF3. By `def:povm-distance` at lines 192-199 and its explicit interpretation at lines 210-212, `A≈_δB` supplies only an `O(δ)` bound. The operator inequalities preserve that hidden constant; they do not prove the literal `≤δ` conclusions at lines 253 and 270. The source repeats the imprecision at `references/qpbt-paper/06_nonlocal_games_and_mipstar.tex:347-380`, labels `fact:add-a-proj2` and `lem:cool-closeness-fact`. Replace both final bounds by `O(δ)`.\\\\n\\\\nF4. The paper fixes `N` as the positive integers at `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:4-7` and takes `m,d,ldc∈N` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:33-35`, label `sec:ld-game`. At `(q,m,d,k)=(2,1,0,1)`, the blueprint's `δ_ld` is zero for every `ε`; taking `ε=1` admits arbitrary strategies, while deterministic players returning different point values contradict the three exact measurement conclusions. Require `d,k≥1`; any harmless `k=0` extension should be a separate corollary.\\\\n\\\\nF5. `def:ld-win-predicate` replaces the paper's ambiguous zero-direction clause with universal quantification over every valid `t`. That is a defensible correction, but line 146 then falsely says the modified game “coincides” with the external tensor-code test. The source proof at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:442-454`, label `lem:ld-soundness`, depends on that identity. Specify a canonical zero-direction test and prove the required monotonicity or soundness transfer.\\\\n\\\\nF6. The paper introduces `q,m,d∈N` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:903-905`; its `def:admissible` at lines 958-960 adds field admissibility and `m|q` within that positive domain. The blueprint instead calls `(2,1,0)` admissible. Then `δ_qld=0` even for `ε=1`, so `thm:pauli` would map an arbitrary product strategy exactly to an EPR-containing state, impossible under local isometries. The honest line answers and `def:combine-map` also cease to have degree at most zero. Add `d≥1` and revise the `d=0` discussion without discarding the corrected probability calculation.\\\\n\\\\nF7. The source answer format at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:330-345`, Figure `fig:ld-decider`, consists of coefficient lists for degree-`d` or degree-`md` univariate polynomials. Defining `deg_md(ℓ)` as functions on the geometric set `ℓ` collapses distinct representatives when the degree is large and collapses every zero-direction parameterization to a single constant function. Consequently the original strategy measurement cannot be indexed as in `def:expanded-line-measurement`, and the universal zero-direction check is lost. Retain parameterized polynomial representatives and explicitly embed degree-`d` ALine outcomes.\\\\n\\\\nF8. The exact last inequality in `lem:povm-to-obs` should be `O(|A|δ)`, and line 869 of `lem:qld-comm-line-cons` should be `O(ε)`. Their approximation conclusions survive after retaining hidden constants, but the displayed proofs do not follow from `def:povm-distance`.\\\\n\\\\nF9. The actual diagonal sampler sets `w=π_{j-1}(v)`, so only coordinates before `j=χ(s)` vanish; `w_j` may vanish and `w=0` has positive probability. Thus line 562's “first nonzero coordinate” assertion is false. Lines 565-570 also choose `s_X,s_Z` without the uniform laws on their `χ`-fibres, while Property 2 mixes distributions on line-point pairs as if they were distributions on lines. Compare `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:230-271` and the inherited defective proof at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1063-1115`, label `lem:qld-sublines`. A complete conditional sampler and coherent marginal statement are required.\\\\n\\\\nF10. The retained estimate is `O(m(ε^(1/4)+δ_P^(1/4)+δ_Q^(1/4)+δ_Line^(1/2)))`, with `δ_Line=√ε`. Taking `ε=m^-4` and admissible `q` sufficiently large makes both advertised arguments `m²ε` and `md/q` tend to zero while `mε^(1/4)=1`. Hence no vanishing function of the advertised variables dominates the proof. The same mismatch occurs between `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1033`, label `lem:qld-4-13`, and lines 1134-1137. Prove the stronger joint-law route or weaken the error statement.\\\\n\\\\nF11. `def:ld-game` requires its dimension to divide `q`, but `lem:qld-4-7` applies it with dimension `2m+2`. Admissibility gives only `m|q`; for power-of-two `m≥2`, `2m+2=2(m+1)` has an odd factor and cannot divide power-of-two `q`. The source makes the same unsupported application at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1278-1288`, label `lem:qld-4-7`. The caveat at lines 919-924 documents the gap but does not prove the lemma; a generalized sampler and soundness theorem are needed.\\\\n\\\\nF12. `lem:qld-unitary` controls `V(M_h⊗I)V†`, whereas the defined isometry satisfies `φM_hφ†=V(M_h⊗|EPR⟩⟨EPR|)V†`. The direct inference at lines 281-289, also present at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1864-1875`, is therefore missing a step. Prove that the difference annihilates the transformed actual state and use projectivity plus its distance from the ideal state to transfer the summed squared estimate.\\\\n\\\\nF13 and F14 are factual PR-record corrections. Exactly five bibliography records are added, and the current successful CI record is for `99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf`, not `2f7aca9`.\\\\n\\\\nThe current local CI record is green for blueprint rendering, synchronization, paper-gap checks, and proof-debt checks. No Lean source, `\\\\\\\\lean` links, or direct proof holes changed. Those checks do not validate the mathematical claims above. Earlier issues concerning the canonical complement, symmetrization, sandwich indexing, graph weights, Reed-Solomon parameters, Pauli sampler, decoder, phases, and the normalization case split are repaired. External Ji2021 soundness details are not mirrored locally, leaving the missing transfer in F5 as residual source risk.\\\\n\\\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\\"}}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n./res