d pair `(u,v)`, and receive two field values. The blueprint instead sends a seeded diagonal line and receives a polynomial. Its nontrivial cross-tests also have mass `2/9`, versus `1/3` in the cited game. A valid reduction must construct pair measurements by postprocessing, handle hidden subcubes and seed fibers while preserving projectivity and synchronicity, and prove the resulting value bound, approximately `rej_tensor ≤ 3/2 rej_ld + O(1/(mq))`. The claimed difference of only `2/(mq)` does not establish this.\\n    40\\t\\n    41\\t**F2.** The same provider theorem requires its auxiliary parameter `K ≥ 12mt`. For the degree-`d` Reed–Solomon code, `t = d+1`, but line 164 takes `K=m³d`, which can be smaller than `12m(d+1)`. Taking `K ≥ max(m³d,12m(d+1))` and redoing the polynomial/exponential error absorption would repair this source-hypothesis omission.\\n    42\\t\\n    43\\t**F3.** The QPBT mirror at [14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:713), label `thm:linearity`, inserts `δ≤1`; [Natarajan–Vidick Theorem 10](https://arxiv.org/html/1610.03574v1) does not. Lines 233–241 then apply the restricted version separately to each `(x,z)`, although a small global average does not imply every conditional defect is at most one. Import the provider statement without this restriction, or supply an explicit good/bad-fiber saturation argument before averaging.\\n    44\\t\\n    45\\t**F4.** The cited proof of Facts 4.13–4.14 at [05_quantum_preliminaries.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/references/neexp-paper/05_quantum_preliminaries.tex:420), lines 420–428, uses `A_a²≤A_a` and `B_a²≤B_a`, giving “at most twice” the off-diagonal mass. Equality is stated only for projective measurements. Replace “leaves exactly twice” accordingly.\\n    46\\t\\n    47\\t**F5–F6.** The divisibility note currently treats removal of the seed as the only game-format mismatch. Its directly indexed game still reveals an index and asks for a polynomial, unlike the cited pair measurement, and its verdict therefore overstates the proposed repair. Moreover, averaging each prover’s line measurement separately changes a seeded synchronicity correlation `E_s⟨M_s⊗N_s⟩` into `E_{s,s'}⟨M_s⊗N_{s'}⟩`; Naimark dilation preserves the latter, not the former. The note must give a faithful source comparison and a transport that actually controls all cross and synchronicity branches.\\n    48\\t\\n    49\\t**F7.** `rem:qld-4-13-source-defects` correctly observes that the source statement at [14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020), label `lem:qld-4-13`, claims `poly(m²ε,md/q)`, while lines 1134–1137 prove only `m·poly(ε,md/q)` and lines 1241–1245 use an unsupported joint-law decomposition. Under [policy.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/docs/paper-gaps/policy.tex:19), lines 19–33 and 121–129, this requires a separate self-contained note and citation.\\n    50\\t\\n    51\\t**F8.** That policy also requires blueprint bibliography entries to carry published URLs at lines 248–252. The comment claiming an `EVOLUTION.md` override has no corresponding protocol entry, while `texra-blueprint.toml` still defines the published site base. Both new entries should use their configured published note URLs.\\n    52\\t\\n    53\\tNo Lean source changed, the sole `\\\\leanok` correspondence matches `Measurement.postprocess`, and the changed mathematical files contain no direct `sorry`, `admit`, or axiom bypass. Chapters 11, 14, and 16 otherwise checked clean; the symmetrization-attainment and final divisibility obligations are explicitly marked. The supplied local CI is green, but 