`[x]` resolved,\\n`[-]` outdated (the cited lines were rewritten; does not block).\\n\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\n- [ ] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:475` — `lem:qld-4-13` treats zero-direction evaluation classes as POVMs, and its proof drops the non-evaluating outcome mass.\\n- [ ] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:115` — `def:ld-meas` conflates polynomial representatives with the paper’s function-indexed outcomes for unrestricted `d`.\\n- [ ] F3 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:577` — `lem:twisted-commutation` uses a field element as an operator exponent and cannot derive the natural `p`-th power as written.\\n- [ ] F4 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:606` — The proof incorrectly invokes `F_q`-linearity of `tr_{q→p}`, which is only `F_p`-linear.\\n- [ ] F5 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:647` — `lem:pauli-observable-expansion` leaves the inversion parameter `b` unquantified.\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:380` — `lem:ortho` cites literal `[ML20]`, leaving its imported proof without a valid bibliographic reference.\\n<!-- findings:end -->\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nChanges are required. These are new findings relative to the existing ledger; the mathematical files at this head are unchanged from the [previous code review](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/4277943db23d2dde26e90908ede8041fb7902e36-code.md:1), whose unresolved findings also remain in force.\\n\\n**F1.** `def:ideg-deg-polynomials` at `ch14:67` states that evaluation classes on a zero-direction line form only a submeasurement, with non-evaluating coefficient-polynomial outcomes assigned to `⊥`. Such lines have positive probability by `ch15:664–672`. Consequently the `\\\\simeq` statement in `lem:qld-4-13` is not between POVMs, and the identity at `ch15:927` omits the `⊥` class. The primary source repeats this unsupported partition in `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1204–1230`, label `claim:17-3`. The proof must complete the family or bound and absorb the missing mass.\\n\\n**F2.** The paper defines polynomials as functions with reduced exponents in `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:836–844`; its `def:ld-meas` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:397–407` is therefore function-indexed. The blueprint instead identifies this with formal `polyfunc` representatives and claims all chapter regimes have `d=1`. Yet `def:ld-game` and `lem:ld-soundness` allow arbitrary positive `d`. Over `F₂` with `d=2`, `X` and `X²` are distinct representatives inducing the same function. Separate the paper-facing measurement class from the Lean representative class, or restrict the identification to `d≤q−1`.\\n\\n/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf-code.md\\n---\\npr: 0001\\nkind: code\\nbranch: issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint\\nbase: main\\nmerge_base: c744e92a45536cb074e51741191dbf5355147ae0\\nhead_sha: 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf\\nverdict: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\nreview_state: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\nsession: reviewer-pr0001-20260830-03\\nmodel: (dispatcher default)\\ngenerated: 2026-08-30T08:29:41Z\\n---\\n\\n# Code review — PR 0001 @ 99d235cf8615\\n\\nLocal replacement for the `code-review` job of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved,\\n`[-]` outdated (the cited lines were rewritten; does not block).\\n\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\n- [-] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:531` — `def:typed-cl-distributions` samples from `μ_G` without the nonempty-edge condition needed to define it.  <!-- outdated at cf4cfa6eb26ad593c4e130d033b54e6a455a1ae1 -->\\n- [-] F2 (b