, label `lem:qld-comm-line-cons`. Complete the families with \\\\(A_\\\\perp=I-\\\\sum_aA_a\\\\) and \\\\(B_\\\\perp=0\\\\), including the already-derived missing-mass bound, or prove an explicit submeasurement analogue.\\n\\nF2 is source-statement drift. The actual Natarajan–Vidick theorem gives exact linearity for every pair but only averaged closeness,\\n\\\\(\\\\mathbb E_u\\\\,\\\\mathrm{DIS}_{\\\\rho'}(\\\\mathcal A(u),A(u))^2\\\\le\\\\delta\\\\), not closeness for every \\\\(u\\\\) ([Theorem 10, Equation (8)](https://arxiv.org/html/1610.03574#S3)). The QPBT mirror misquotes it at `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:713-724`, label `thm:linearity`; the blueprint must not inherit that strengthening. Restate the closeness on average and update `rem:linearity-import`. `lem:qld-4-10` already uses only the averaged form at lines 212–215.\\n/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3-code.md\\n---\\npr: 0001\\nkind: code\\nbranch: issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint\\nbase: main\\nmerge_base: c744e92a45536cb074e51741191dbf5355147ae0\\nhead_sha: 2f7aca9ede9a01c06bf3b337d5187f4160d292d3\\nverdict: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\nreview_state: CHANGES_REQUESTED\\nsession: reviewer-pr0001-20260830-01\\nmodel: (dispatcher default)\\ngenerated: 2026-08-30T06:56:19Z\\n---\\n\\n# Code review — PR 0001 @ 2f7aca9ede9a\\n\\nLocal replacement for the `code-review` job of `.github/workflows/pr-review.yml`.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\nCheckbox states: `[ ]` unresolved (blocks the merge), `[x]` resolved,\\n`[-]` outdated (the cited lines were rewritten; does not block).\\n\\n<!-- findings:begin -->\\n- [-] F1 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch11_qpbt_algebra.tex:98` — `def:canonical-complement` falsely claims that the RREF complement depends on the chosen basis.  <!-- outdated at 99d235cf861527bc3def2e843a9ff85b12985bdf -->\\n- [-] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch1