 — `lem:pauli-observable-expansion` leaves the inversion parameter `b` unquantified.\\n- [ ] F6 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch14_qpbt_observables.tex:380` — `lem:ortho` cites literal `[ML20]`, leaving its imported proof without a valid bibliographic reference.\\n\\n## Review\\n\\nChanges are required. This same-SHA re-review carries forward the six exact-head findings because the local protocol replaces that ledger. I found no additional code finding beyond the existing ledgers. The mathematical files are unchanged from the [previous code review](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/4277943db23d2dde26e90908ede8041fb7902e36-code.md:25), whose eight unresolved findings remain in force. The [exact-head prose review](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/b91e9bb01bd2e5f48a00a0750f53480e241b8576-prose.md:25) also remains unresolved.\\n\\n**F1.** `def:ideg-deg-polynomials` explicitly says that, on a zero-direction line, the classes indexed by `a ∈ F_q` form only a submeasurement and require an additional `⊥` outcome. Such lines occur with positive probability. Nevertheless, `lem:qld-4-13` applies POVM consistency to only the `F_q` classes, and the identity at line 927 similarly omits `⊥`. Complete the family or bound and absorb the missing mass. The source repeats this gap in `references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1204`, label `claim:17-3`.\\n\\n**F2.** The source defines polynomials as reduced polynomial functions at `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:836` and uses function-indexed outcomes in `def:ld-meas` at `references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:397`. The blueprint instead uses unrestricted formal representatives while `lem:ld-soundness` permits arbitrary positive `d`. Over `F₂`, `X` and `X²` are distinct representatives but the same function. Separate the paper-facing measurement class or restrict the identification to `d≤q−1`.\\n\\n**F3.** Both the source and blueprint write `(τ^W(a))^b` for `b∈F_p`, although operator exponentiation requires a natural or integer exponent. Moreover, substituting the field element `p=0` cannot establish the natural `p`-fold power. State the iteration law for `r∈N` using `(r mod p)·a`, then derive the `p`-th-power identity.\\n\\n**F4–F5.** The trace `tr_{q→p}` is `F_p`-linear, not `F_q`-linear; additivity is sufficient for the phase calculation. The Fourier inversion identity must also explicitly quantify `b∈F_q^n`, matching `references/qpbt-paper/04_preliminaries.tex:1156`.\\n\\n**F6.** Replace literal `[ML20]` with the available `Ji2020LowIndividualDegree` citation key and identify the orthonormalization provider, whose proof begins at `references/ldt-paper/orthonormalization.tex:282`.\\n\\nI reviewed committed head `b91e9bb`; staged working-copy repairs were excluded and therefore do not resolve or outdate these findings. `git diff --check` is clean, no Lean source changed, and no direct proof hole or integrity bypass was introduced.\\n\\nVERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
